From 8361fe807b646197512086c00f9cd1581c4651d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:21:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] rk3326: load rk915 for its device tree node

The rk915 driver powers the chip itself (no mmc-pwrseq): the SDIO card
it binds to only appears once the module is loaded. The module was only
ever loaded through that card's SDIO modalias, i.e. only when the chip
happened to be powered at boot, and RK3326 has no modules.conf.

A modprobe alias on the OF modalias of the rockchip,rk915 node (R36
Ultra, XiFan RF35H) makes udev load it when that platform device
appears, whatever the state of the power line. Boards without the node
never match it.

Signed-off-by: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019W6m4A3E7pevQ1bs91jPmM
---
 .../rockchip/rk3326/fsoverlay/etc/modprobe.d/rk915.conf      | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/fsoverlay/etc/modprobe.d/rk915.conf

diff --git a/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/fsoverlay/etc/modprobe.d/rk915.conf b/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/fsoverlay/etc/modprobe.d/rk915.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d4700b6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/fsoverlay/etc/modprobe.d/rk915.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# The rk915 Wi-Fi driver powers the chip itself, and its SDIO card only
+# appears afterwards: if the chip is off at boot, nothing would load the
+# module. Load it for the rockchip,rk915 device tree node instead (R36 Ultra,
+# XiFan RF35H); boards without that node never match.
+alias of:N*T*Crockchip,rk915* rk915
